description:
Change under review: add a `--reset` flag to the settings command. Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file, including its imports of `saveSettings`, `DEFAULT_SETTINGS`, `printSettings`, and `log`, is unchanged and compiles.

`src/settings/store.ts` (unchanged, shown for context):
```ts
10 export function saveSettings(path: string, settings: Settings): ResultAsync<void, SettingsError> {
11   return ResultAsync.fromPromise(Bun.write(path, JSON.stringify(settings)), (cause) => ({ type: "WriteFailed", cause }));
12 }
```

`src/commands/settings.ts` (changed, lines 30-37):
```ts
30 export async function runSettings(args: SettingsArgs): Promise<number> {
31   if (args.reset) {
32     saveSettings(args.path, DEFAULT_SETTINGS);
33     log.info("settings reset");
34     return 0;
35   }
36   return printSettings(args.path);
37 }
```

`src/commands/__tests__/settings.test.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { expect, spyOn, test } from "bun:test";
2 import * as store from "../../settings/store.js";
3 import { runSettings } from "../settings.js";
4
5 test("reset writes defaults", async () => {
6   const spy = spyOn(store, "saveSettings");
7   expect(await runSettings({ reset: true, path: "settings.json" })).toBe(0);
8   expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalled();
9 });
```
